Apache-2.0 is chosen deliberately. A foundational standard cannot be copyleft --
it would prevent adoption in commercial robotics stacks, which is where a
standard has to live. It also keeps this work clearly separated from GADEN,
which is LGPL-3.0: every equation here is implemented from the published
literature (Farrell et al. 2002), not transcribed from GADEN source.
